  "goodToKnow": "Die Schadenfreude is the pleasure you feel at another person's misfortune, from Schaden (harm) and Freude (joy). English borrowed the word unchanged, because it had no single term for it. The adjective is schadenfroh, and an old saying has it that Schadenfreude ist die reinste Freude. The word has no plural, and it usually appears with empfinden, spüren or verbergen."
